      "role": "user",
      "content": "fair enough. but when you say they might argue for a \"predictable environment,\" isn't that just a fancy way of saying they want to keep things exactly as they are so they don't have to change? it feels like the \"risk to innovation\" argument is always used by the winners to stop anyone else from playing the game. if we actually look at the economic data, shouldn't the priority be consumer choice and preventing market capture rather than protecting the specific business models of multibillion dollar corporations?",
